    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d133">

                <pb facs="0232" n="130" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg130"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15A5/512: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bingham</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-10-24T21:00:00-05:00">October 24, 1935—9
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>315. Department’s 313, October 24, 7 p.m. When conveying to the British
                    Government our acceptance of their invitation, you should inform them that of
                    course we are accepting on the assumption that the British agreed to the
                    position taken in our last cable giving the Navy Department basis for
                        agreement<anchor n="84" xml:id="d133-f1"/> and also, notwithstanding the
                    fact that it may not be possible to agree now on quantitative limitations, that
                    it is still to be understood that we both agree on the principle of naval parity
                    as between the United States and the British Empire.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d133-f1" n="84" xml:id="d133-f1-content">
                <p>See Department’s telegram No. 300, October 14, 6 p.m., <ref target="#pg125">p.
                        125</ref>.</p>
            </note>
